NAME
    printf - write formatted text and escape sequences

SYNOPSIS
    printf FORMAT [ARG...]

DESCRIPTION
    Writes FORMAT without adding a newline. C-style escapes in FORMAT include
    \\, \a, \b, \e, \f, \n, \r, \t, \v, octal, hexadecimal, and Unicode
    escapes. \c stops output. %% writes %, %s writes an argument, and %b writes
    an argument after interpreting its escapes. FORMAT repeats to consume extra
    arguments used by %s or %b.
